.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_PUT_U64 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_put_u8 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_u16 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_u32 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_u64 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_i8 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_i16 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_i32 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_i64 ,
.Nm dtfl_put_bytes ,
.Nm dtfl_get_u8 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_u16 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_u32 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_u64 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_i8 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_i16 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_i32 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_i64 ,
.Nm dtfl_get_bytes
.Nd encode and decode built-in record values
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/record.h
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_u8 "void *buf" "uint8_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_u16 "void *buf" "uint16_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_u32 "void *buf" "uint32_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_u64 "void *buf" "uint64_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_i8 "void *buf" "int8_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_i16 "void *buf" "int16_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_i32 "void *buf" "int32_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_i64 "void *buf" "int64_t v"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_put_bytes "void *buf" "const void *p" "size_t n"
.Ft uint8_t
.Fn dtfl_get_u8 "const void *buf"
.Ft uint16_t
.Fn dtfl_get_u16 "const void *buf"
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn dtfl_get_u32 "const void *buf"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn dtfl_get_u64 "const void *buf"
.Ft int8_t
.Fn dtfl_get_i8 "const void *buf"
.Ft int16_t
.Fn dtfl_get_i16 "const void *buf"
.Ft int32_t
.Fn dtfl_get_i32 "const void *buf"
.Ft int64_t
.Fn dtfl_get_i64 "const void *buf"
.Ft const void *
.Fn dtfl_get_bytes "const void *buf" "size_t *n"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions write and read the encodings of the built-in record
types in
.Xr dtfl_type 3 ,
so callers handle native values.
The encodings preserve order: comparing two encoded integers with
.Xr memcmp 3
gives the same answer as comparing the integers.
.Pp
The unsigned
.Fn dtfl_put_u*
functions write
.Fa v
big-endian in 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes.
The signed
.Fn dtfl_put_i*
functions write the two's complement value big-endian with its sign bit
flipped, so that -1 encodes as
.Li 7f ff ...
and 0 as
.Li 80 00 ... .
Each
.Fn dtfl_get_*
reads a value of its type's width from
.Fa buf
and undoes the encoding.
.Fa buf
need not be aligned.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_put_bytes
writes a
.Vt bytes
or
.Vt string
value: a u64 big-endian length
.Fa n ,
then
.Fa n
bytes from
.Fa p .
.Fn dtfl_get_bytes
reads one back, storing the payload length in
.Fa *n .
It does not validate; check untrusted input with
.Xr dtfl_type_value_len 3
first.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn dtfl_put_*
functions return the number of bytes written: the type's width, or
.Fa n
+ 8 for
.Fn dtfl_put_bytes .
The caller must provide that much room.
.Fn dtfl_get_bytes
returns a pointer to the payload inside
.Fa buf .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
unsigned char a[4], b[4];

dtfl_put_i32(a, -5);
dtfl_put_i32(b, 3);
assert(memcmp(a, b, 4) < 0);
assert(dtfl_get_i32(a) == -5);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
None.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_type 3
.Sh HISTORY
Rust serializes records with bincode, which is little-endian and does
not preserve order.
libdtfl chooses order-preserving encodings so that the built-in
comparisons are byte comparisons.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
All of these functions are reentrant.
